# The Incremental and the Iterativ

Alistair Cockburn put this on a mug

> Incremental (development) supports the process
> Iterative (development) supports the product

OK, so I'm not going to pay to find out what that means. But I think I
can work it out. Which, in a way, should be more enlightening.

So (thumbnail version)

Iterative - each time delivering some working version of mona lisa

Incremental - each time delivering a bit of mona lisa

---

Iterative supports product because, at each iteration, assumptions can
be tested through use and the feedback can go iinto improving the
product in further iterations. And you may discover that you've
already "won".

Incremental supports development _process_ because it "knife and
forks" a problem.
